I go back to the clothes.
I see a blue top.
It is a cotton top.
It is a good top.
I take that top.
I go to the fitting room.
I wear that blue top.
I look in the mirror.
This top is very small.
This is a small top.
I remove that top.
I come outside.
The saleswoman looks at me.
She asks, "Is the top good?"
I say, "No, this is a small top."
"This blue top is very small for me."
"I want a big top."
I give that blue top back.
I look at other clothes.
